1
01:10:51,350 --> 01:10:55,059
But I must've been knocked out, because the
maid tells me Miss Van Gorder is missing.

2
01:10:55,993 --> 01:10:57,983
You better call Anderson and let him know.

3
01:10:58,979 --> 01:11:00,879
He's not at home? Well, where is he?

4
01:11:02,145 --> 01:11:03,954
Out on a case? What case?

5
01:11:05,024 --> 01:11:06,321
Dr. Wells?

6
01:11:07,165 --> 01:11:08,552
What else did they tell you about him?

7
01:11:08,778 --> 01:11:12,170
Oh hurry, will you?
We got to find Miss Cornelia!

8
01:11:14,235 --> 01:11:15,125
Ok.

9
01:11:15,924 --> 01:11:17,944
Lieutenant Anderson is out on a case.

10
01:11:18,291 --> 01:11:21,939
Dr. Wells was found dead in a
room next to his garage, murdered.

11
01:11:22,964 --> 01:11:24,471
Dr. Wells?

12
01:11:24,728 --> 01:11:26,510
There's something
queer about the killing of

13
01:11:26,534 --> 01:11:28,316
Wells but headquarters
won't talk about it.

14
01:11:28,617 --> 01:11:31,692
Lizzie, Warner isn't in his room,
there's no sign of him anywhere.

15
01:11:31,722 --> 01:11:33,758
And I was supposed to
keep an eye on that guy.

16
01:11:33,788 --> 01:11:36,819
Where is Miss Cornelia?
That's what I want to know!

17
01:11:36,999 --> 01:11:40,663
Wait a minute, didn't you say that the chain
and the bolt were off of the front door?

18
01:11:40,693 --> 01:11:43,843
- I certainly did.
- Well, maybe Miss Van Gorder went outside.

19
01:11:43,873 --> 01:11:46,737
Oh, she never would, we better look.

20
01:11:47,973 --> 01:11:52,707
I can't, I can't breathe, there's no air.

21
01:12:00,743 --> 01:12:02,281
Miss Cornelia?

22
01:12:02,537 --> 01:12:04,617
- Miss Van Gorder?
- Miss Cornelia?

23
01:12:04,647 --> 01:12:06,366
- Miss Cornelia?
- Miss Van Gorder?

24
01:12:06,396 --> 01:12:10,248
Look, there's a light in that
room on the third floor.

25
01:12:10,896 --> 01:12:12,064
Were you up there tonight?

26
01:12:12,094 --> 01:12:15,268
Well, of course I was, but I turned the
lights out before I came downstairs.

27
01:12:15,298 --> 01:12:17,528
Miss Cornelia might've
turned them on again.

28
01:12:17,558 --> 01:12:19,790
That's where we're
going to look first, come on.

29
01:12:40,911 --> 01:12:44,861
Cornelia? Cornelia?

30
01:12:46,281 --> 01:12:50,758
- Miss Cornelia?
- Yes I'm, I'm here.

31
01:12:54,617 --> 01:12:57,557
Right here!

32
01:13:01,072 --> 01:13:03,209
Here we are Miss Van
Gorder, what do we do now?

33
01:13:03,525 --> 01:13:07,083
Over the mantle, there are five panels.

34
01:13:07,640 --> 01:13:10,625
Strike it, with your hands.

35
01:13:15,027 --> 01:13:19,067
- Which panel did you say Miss Van Gorder?
- Oh I, I just...

36
01:13:20,439 --> 01:13:23,379
Miss Van Gorder, which panel?
We couldn't hear you!

37
01:13:23,409 --> 01:13:28,128
She said strike it, what difference does
it make which panel? Strike them all.

38
01:13:30,811 --> 01:13:31,881
Look!

39
01:13:45,033 --> 01:13:51,945
Oh, it's all right now,
it's all right dear, Lizzie's here.

40
01:13:57,779 --> 01:13:59,301
- Feeling better?
- Yes, much better.

41
01:13:59,331 --> 01:14:00,256
We'll take you to your room.

42
01:14:00,266 --> 01:14:03,293
Oh, no you wont, I'm going to
stay right here, I'm quite all right.

43
01:14:03,875 --> 01:14:07,119
Oh, how blessed it is to
breathe without an effort, you know...

44
01:14:07,435 --> 01:14:12,278
no one knows how sweet the air can taste
until someone shuts it off for a moment.

45
01:14:12,641 --> 01:14:14,829
That room is just like a box.

46
01:14:15,432 --> 01:14:19,138
When the mantle piece closed, it
seemed like all the air was drawn out of it.

47
01:14:19,716 --> 01:14:21,089
Look, there's goes again!

48
01:14:21,340 --> 01:14:23,531
Let it close, I can open it from in here.

49
01:14:28,016 --> 01:14:30,358
There's a control
panel behind this blueprint.

50
01:14:30,998 --> 01:14:33,086
Electric motor under the trap door here.

51
01:14:33,508 --> 01:14:35,681
Once the door is open
you can keep it that way.
